17592186730892 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186730904 #edb/ref 13194139543428 #edb/ref 17592186576411 true] [#edb/ref 17592186730892 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0301e25f-6155-52ff-a274-7e2037467423" #edb/ref 13194139543428 #edb/ref 17592186576411 true] [#edb/ref 17592186730893 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186730892 #edb/ref 13194139543428 #edb/ref 17592186576411 true] [#edb/ref 17592186730893 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 13194139543428 #edb/ref 17592186576411 true] [#edb/ref 17592186730893 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the slope $m$ of $y=h(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ if\n\n$$\nh(x)=\\frac{-\\cot x}{\\sin x}.\n$$\n\n$m=$ {{field-1}}" #edb/ref 13194139543428 #edb/ref 17592186576411 true] [#edb/ref 17592186730893 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0bfef524-e604-5fc5-ad6f-7b59528ae372" #edb/ref 13194139543428 #edb/ref 17592186576411 true] [#edb/ref 17592186730893 #edb/ref 1074 "The slope is $m=h'\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)$. The numerator and denominator both vary with $x$. Using the quotient rule, with $u=-\\cot x$ and $v=\\sin x$, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nh'(x)&=\\frac{u'v-uv'}{v^2}\\\\\n &=\\frac{\\csc^2 x\\sin x+\\cot x\\cos x}{\\sin^2 x}\\\\\n &=\\frac{\\csc x+\\cot x\\cos x}{\\sin^2 x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe plus sign comes from subtracting $(-\\cot x)\\cos x$. At $x=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$, use $\\sin x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$, $\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}$, $\\cot x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$, and $\\csc x=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm&=\\frac{\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^2}\\\\\n &=\\frac{\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{3}}}{\\frac{3}{4}}\\\\\n &=\\frac{10}{3\\sqrt{3}}\\\\\n &=\\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{9}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)\\ne0$, the original function and this derivative are defined at the requested input." #edb/ref 13194139543428 #edb/ref 17592186576411 true] [#edb/ref 17592186730894 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-\\frac{4\\pi}{9}" #edb/ref 13194139543428 #edb/r